From 7ec2996ddf34b435a54ce2078f395f08c6335934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:52:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08129/11362] [outer-loop] Audit the ARC induce prompt: not
 truncated, but misdirected

Diagnoses the induce prompt against the three named hypotheses (starved /
misdirected / asked the impossible). 24 of 25 public games; dc22 is an honest
coverage gap (no induction window), never a zero. No LLM, no GPU, no weights --
tokenized with the live generator's own vocabulary via vocab_only.

Fidelity gate: 19/19 rendered prompts reproduce the frozen
arc_goal_predicate_anatomy_20260801 shas byte-identically.

NOT STARVED BY TRUNCATION. Worst-case payload 8,866 tokens against a
16,384-token per-slot budget (54.1%); nothing truncates and the 40,000-char
transition budget never binds. Corrects a documented claim: the k=8 cap loses at
least one whole action on 10 of 24 games, where _induce_transitions_k's docstring
states action coverage was not being lost (checked on six games, stated for all).

MISDIRECTED. The payload's FIRST instruction is /no_think + "Do NOT analyze the
grids" + "Skip all reasoning", present on 24/24 -- it forbids the inference the
task requires, and was justified against a generator retired 2026-07-28. Output
contract is full-grid on 24/24 while all evidence is delta-encoded; a median
40.7% of tokens is one static layout grid.

IDENTITY IS INVITED, forbidden by none: identity is cell-wise correct on a median
98.96% of cells; a median 2 of 7 declared actions are ever observed (11/24 games
show exactly one, 0/24 show all seven); 0/24 prompts forbid a do-nothing engine.

GOAL PROMPT IS EMPTY, not starved: 96 tokens on 23/24 games, 0/24 carry a grid or
a transition, against the induce prompt's median 3,717.

Corrects the brief's premise: only 3 of 27 on-disk engines are behaviourally
identity, not the population -- 12 return the parameter everywhere but write
through it in place. The stronger surviving measure is the empty-branch rate
(15/27 at 1.0). ft09 shows why: a correct click-dispatch with eight colour cases
and every consequent left as `return grid`. The model does the perception and
dispatch and fails only at naming each case's outcome.

Diagnosis only. Nothing changed: no prompt edited, no flag flipped,
results/arc_e3 read and never written. No behavioural claim -- no action, plan,
level or engine accuracy was measured.

